,50664117,50664483,50664772,50665412],"created_at":"2026-11-26T17:11:29Z","created_at_i":1795713089,"num_comments":101,"objectID":"50657265","points":415,"story_id":50657265,"title":"AMD-specific fork of llama.cpp","updated_at":"2026-11-27T16:54:46Z","url":"https://devnull.land/amd-specific-llama-cpp"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"ritzaco"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Google Will Make AI Agents Use Its MCP Servers. The Gmail One Can't Send Email"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://techstackups.com/articles/google-workspace-ai-agents-mcp/"}},"_tags":["story","author_ritzaco","story_50653477","front_page"],"author":"ritzaco","children":[50653883,50653905,50653914,50653988,50654002,50654029,50654031,50654039,50654042,50654055,50654073,50654099,50654101,50654102,50654119,50654136,50654171,50654225,50654266,50654290,50654300,50654314,50654322,50654332,50654382,50654421,50654440,50654443,50654452,50654529,50654593,50654766,50654843,50654962,50655218,50655301,50655891,50656054,50656224,50656238,50656512,50658672,50658725,50658785,50658803,50658840,50659024,50659171,50659303,50659598,50659717,50659962,50660063,50660526,50660559,50661222,50661312,50661404,50661571,50661788,50661803,50661939,50662534,50662570,50662595,50662645,50662828,50663021,50663526,50663581,50663849,50663895,50664868,50665027,50665414,50665500,50665749,50665881,50667236,50667521,50667589,50667695,50668199],"created_at":"2026-11-26T09:44:23Z","created_at_i":1795686263,"num_comments":321,"objectID":"50653477","points":394,"story_id":50653477,"title":"Google Will Make AI Agents Use Its MCP Servers. The Gmail One Can't Send Email","updated_at":"2026-11-27T16:54:19Z","url":"https://techstackups.com/articles/google-workspace-ai-agents-mcp/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Bender"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"CTO of 'RansomwareHelp' indicted for wire fraud"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://krebsonsecurity.com/2026/11/cto-of-ransomwarehelp-indicted-for-wire-fraud/"}},"_tags":["story","author_Bender","story_50657645","front_page"],"author":"Bender","children":[50657797,50657967,50658045,50658167,50658276,50658367,50658541,50658618,50658789,50658920,50659055,50659653,50659836,50660319,50663044,50663287,50663564,50664131,50664520],"created_at":"2026-11-26T17:47:45Z","created_at_i":1795715265,"num_comments":157,"objectID":"50657645","points":318,"story_id":50657645,"title":"CTO of 'RansomwareHelp' indicted for wire fraud","updated_at":"2026-11-27T16:48:02Z","url":"https://krebsonsecurity.com/2026/11/cto-of-ransomwarehelp-indicted-for-wire-fraud/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"thanato0s"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"I'm glad to announce that I'm releasing my new book, Learning to Play Vim.<p>When I started using Vim more than a decade ago, I wished there was a manual out there teaching how to use this fantastic editor step by step, beginning with the foundations up to more advanced features. Of course at the time I did the vimtutor, but it was too dense for me to remember much from it. I also read the entire Vim manual (`:help manual`), but I didn't like it: it was too detailed in places (for example `02.8 Finding help` completely lost me for a while), and other features didn't get the treatment they deserved.<p>So I decided to write my own Vim manual. It took me more than 4 years and 2987 focused pomodoros (1244 hours) of work to finally get it done!<p>The result:<p>- 21 chapters showing the most important Vim features step by step.<p>- 170 exercises with solutions.<p>- Many real-life examples to show how Vim can be used and configured for your own needs.<p>- The related Vim's help pages to dig further into each feature.<p>Most configs are both written in Vimscript and Lua for Neovim users. This book explores the common features between Vim and Neovim, so don't expect anything about Neovim-specific features (like treesitter or LSP for example).<p>- The landing page: <a href=\"https://themouseless.dev/vim/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://themouseless.dev/vim/</a><p>- A sample of the book with the entire table of contents and the first three chapters covering most of the basics: <a href=\"https://themouseless.dev/content/learning_to_play_vim_sample.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://themouseless.dev/content/learning_to_play_vim_sample...</a>.<p>I wrote this with my bare hands, no LLM involved to spoil the fun."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: I wrote an entire Vim manual over 4 years"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://themouseless.dev/vim/"}},"_tags":["story","author_thanato0s","story_50655868","show_hn","front_page"],"author":"thanato0s","children":[50659031,50659060,50659197,50659635,50660378,50660592,50661419,50661447,50661678,50662782,50662998,50663102,50663721,50663937,50663968,50664458,50665710,50666770,50667262,50667950,50668851],"created_at":"2026-11-26T14:44:22Z","created_at_i":1795704262,"num_comments":89,"objectID":"50655868","points":268,"story_id":50655868,"story_text":"I&#x27;m glad to announce that I&#x27;m releasing my new book, Learning to Play Vim.<p>When I started using Vim more than a decade ago, I wished there was a manual out there teaching how to use this fantastic editor step by step, beginning with the foundations up to more advanced features. Of course at the time I did the vimtutor, but it was too dense for me to remember much from it. I also read the entire Vim manual (`:help manual`), but I didn&#x27;t like it: it was too detailed in places (for example `02.8 Finding help` completely lost me for a while), and other features didn&#x27;t get the treatment they deserved.<p>So I decided to write my own Vim manual. It took me more than 4 years and 2987 focused pomodoros (1244 hours) of work to finally get it done!<p>The result:<p>- 21 chapters showing the most important Vim features step by step.<p>- 170 exercises with solutions.<p>- Many real-life examples to show how Vim can be used and configured for your own needs.<p>- The related Vim&#x27;s help pages to dig further into each feature.<p>Most configs are both written in Vimscript and Lua for Neovim users. This book explores the common features between Vim and Neovim, so don&#x27;t expect anything about Neovim-specific features (like treesitter or LSP for example).<p>- The landing page: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;vim&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;vim&#x2F;</a><p>- A sample of the book with the entire table of contents and the first three chapters covering most of the basics: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;content&#x2F;learning_to_play_vim_sample.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;themouseless.dev&#x2F;content&#x2F;learning_to_play_vim_sample...</a>.<p>I wrote this with my bare hands, no LLM involved to spoil the fun.","title":"Show HN: I wrote an entire Vim manual over 4 years","updated_at":"2026-11-27T16:54:46Z","url":"http://themouseless.dev/vim/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"f_allwein"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Buy Nothing Day \u2013 Friday November 27th 2026"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://www.buynothingday.co.uk/"}},"_tags":["story","author_f_allwein","story_50663261","front_page"],"author":"f_allwein","children":[50663580,50664047,50664293,50664421,50664897,50665119,50665265,50665404,50665727,50665729,50665801,50665928,50666189,50666564,50666639,50666691,50667105,50667215,50667405,50667772,50667872,50667973,50668147,50668150],"created_at":"2026-11-27T05:52:42Z","created_at_i":1795758762,"num_comments":81,"objectID":"50663261","points":268,"story_id":50663261,"title":"Buy Nothing Day \u20