:46Z","url":"https://news.sky.com/story/us-air-forces-cloud-computing-platform-hacked-13617163"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"yuvadam"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"A Deterministic Subexponential-Time Algorithm for the Discrete Logarithm Problem [pdf]"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/3020.pdf"}},"_tags":["story","author_yuvadam","story_50665968","front_page"],"author":"yuvadam","children":[50666173,50666199,50666215,50666220,50666238,50666239,50666260,50666268,50666385,50666407,50666560,50666669,50666749,50666892,50667060,50667239,50667298,50667750,50668357],"created_at":"2026-11-27T12:08:51Z","created_at_i":1795781331,"num_comments":75,"objectID":"50665968","points":166,"story_id":50665968,"title":"A Deterministic Subexponential-Time Algorithm for the Discrete Logarithm Problem [pdf]","updated_at":"2026-11-27T16:54:46Z","url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/3020.pdf"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"mday404"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"a ball will fall. trade on where it lands.<p>I made this game! Some technical details:<p>The entire drop of the ball is simulated server-side, then streamed to each client as server-sent events with a small buffer. Every drop is deterministic from its starting position, so rounds can be replayed exactly for later analysis, but tiny variations in starting position can change the ultimate outcome.<p>There's some AI traders to keep the market moving, but they drop out in any round that has more than five people. They operate using a naive set of rules that I wrote for them, so they're not too hard to beat -- it's when the market is full of real people that it gets tricky.<p>Curious to get feedback on anything you would change, and especially whether the mechanics were clear right away or not."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: bouncemarket \u2013 a live prediction market game for a bouncing ball"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://bouncemarket.minhanhday.com/"}},"_tags":["story","author_mday404","story_50667726","show_hn","front_page"],"author":"mday404","children":[50667813,50667849,50667889,50667972,50668006,50668007,50668037,50668043,50668054,50668059,50668064,50668083,50668096,50668112,50668184,50668217,50668258,50668346,50668367,50668451,50668483,50668604,50668637,50668674,50668694,50668724,50668803,50668812],"created_at":"2026-11-27T15:01:50Z","created_at_i":1795791710,"num_comments":42,"objectID":"50667726","points":150,"story_id":50667726,"story_text":"a ball will fall. trade on where it lands.<p>I made this game! Some technical details:<p>The entire drop of the ball is simulated server-side, then streamed to each client as server-sent events with a small buffer. Every drop is deterministic from its starting position, so rounds can be replayed exactly for later analysis, but tiny variations in starting position can change the ultimate outcome.<p>There&#x27;s some AI traders to keep the market moving, but they drop out in any round that has more than five people. They operate using a naive set of rules that I wrote for them, so they&#x27;re not too hard to beat -- it&#x27;s when the market is full of real people that it gets tricky.<p>Curious to get feedback on anything you would change, and especially whether the mechanics were clear right away or not.","title":"Show HN: bouncemarket \u2013 a live prediction market game for a bouncing ball","updated_at":"2026-11-27T16:54:46Z","url":"https://bouncemarket.minhanhday.com/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"theanonymousone"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Kimi for Science: More scientific ideas, made possible"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://www.kimi.ai/news/kimi-for-science-program"